## Lore

Power Leeches look harmless, even cute: they resemble small human
children, with oversized heads, big innocent eyes, round bellies and thin
limbs, and they stay playful and curious however old they get. That look
hides one of the most dangerous D-Bees on Earth.

They feed on energy, soaking it up through every pore: electricity from
batteries and machines, the power of reactors and E-Clips, ley line
energy and the P.P.E. of spellcasters. Their home world is constantly
battered by solar flares, radiation and ley line storms, and this is how
they survive there. About a hundred were torn away to Rifts Earth by a
ley line storm and, knowing no way home, have learned to live on whatever
energy they find.

On Earth a leech that gorges swells in size, strength and toughness, so
shooting one with energy weapons or spells only makes it stronger. It can
empty a vital machine or a mage, and a really greedy one may grow as big
and as mighty as a dragon before the excess burns off and it shrinks back
to normal within two days.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character and NPC, with a
note that it was not originally designed for players; allowing one is
entirely the G.M.''s decision, and the player should not abuse its powers.

Money also includes 2D4x1,000 credits in tradeable or Black Market items.
A Power Leech can do very well as a town champion, lawman, bounty hunter
or mercenary. It eats sweets and salty snacks for the taste only.

Size 3-4 feet (0.9 to 1.2 m). Weight 50-80 lbs (22.5 to 36 kg). Life span
3D6+75 years; mature by 11. NPC experience level 1D6.

Habitat: anywhere, and scattered across the Megaverse. Fewer than 200 are
thought to be on Rifts Earth as of 109 P.A., a third of them wandering
North America, the Magic Zone above all. Most clans that came to Earth
have sworn allegiance to Psyscape. Enemies: none as such.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'power-leech');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'power-leech';

